      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dr. Talbott laid out Thornport in 1839, digging a private feeder canal that linked Thorn Township to the Licking Summit Reservoir.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thornport%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Thornport’s “port” name comes from its lakeside spot on Buckeye Lake, one of three villages bordering the lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thornport%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A lone log cabin remains in Thornport, a tangible reminder of its pioneer days and bustling canal trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thornport%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A mid‑1800s storm damaged the canal, but the later railroad revived Thornport as a key transport hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Thornport,_Ohio",
